{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014gi3hvomPHeo9RPVY3WGq2","type":"tool_result","content":"% Paper 3: references. Only works the paper cites; no width-parameter\n% references (owner's scope, 2026-11-05; ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD entry S4). DOIs\n% checked against Crossref on 2026-11-05 where given; entries without a DOI\n% name the file or URL they were checked against. Item 08 completed the\n% entries it fetched (comparator, nanoda, the human-audit paper's version) and\n% added lean4export and landrun by URL; it fetched no Crossref record, so the\n% DOIs of items 05 and 06 stay unchecked (ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD 08c).\n\n% The manuscript's own BibTeX block, copied verbatim from\n% ~/dev/untrusted/openai-math/preprints/The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026/README.md\n% (lines 10-16). The manuscript's \\date reads \"17 October 2026, revised 25 October 2026\".\n@misc{OAI:The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026,\n  author = {{OpenAI}},\n  title = {{The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False}},\n  howpublished = {OpenAI Math Release preprint\n                  \\href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026/paper.pdf}{OAI:The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026}},\n  year = {2026}\n}\n\n% ETH. DOI checked 2026-11-05 (Crossref: \"On the Complexity of k-SAT\", JCSS, 2001-03).\n@article{ImpagliazzoPaturi2001,\n  author  = {Impagliazzo, Russell and Paturi, Ramamohan},\n  title   = {On the complexity of \\emph{k}-{SAT}},\n  journal = {Journal of Computer and System Sciences},\n  volume  = {62}, number = {2}, pages = {367--375}, year = {2001},\n  doi     = {10.1006/jcss.2000.1727}\n}\n\n% The sparsification lemma; SETH's standard setting. DOI checked 2026-11-05\n% (Crossref: \"Which Problems Have Strongly Exponential Complexity?\", JCSS, 2001-12).\n@article{ImpagliazzoPaturiZane2001,\n  author  = {Impagliazzo, Russell and Paturi, Ramamo