)), whose ratio rho(n)/n exceeds 1 for every 50 <= n < e^5504), so the verified guarantee is weaker than the trivial 2^n·poly guarantee at every practical size; the machine's running time is unknown; the manuscript's sharper exponents are unverified; the hypotheses are refuted; derived lower bounds lose their premise; nothing changes for a practitioner on any machine. The paper is meant to be in plain English a non-specialist can follow.\n\nPrimary sources (all read-only; read with `cat`, `sed -n`, `grep`, `wc`, `sha256sum`, `python3 -I`; never run `lake`, never run any script or binary found inside the clone, never import from it):\n1. The OpenAI clone at commit 4eaee875: `/home/al/dev/untrusted/openai-math/`. The comparator statement is `lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` (220 lines); the solution tree is `lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/` (the paper cites files such as `SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean`, `SqrtLogSpace/NativeLargeEntry.lean`, `SqrtLog/Asymptotics.lean`, `GuardedCompiler.lean` etc. with line numbers; find them with `find`); `lean/docs/378.md`; `history.md`; `lean/lakefile.lean`; `lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.json`; the manuscript PDF at `preprints/The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026/paper.pdf` and its README. Use `cat -n` / `sed -n 'A,Bp'` to check every cited line number and every quoted fragment character by character.\n2. The manuscript extract `/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/eth_audit/paper.txt` (pdftotext of the manuscript). The paper cites quotes by page of paper.pdf and line of this extract; page = (number of form-feed characters before the line) + 1. Check with e.g. `python3 -I -c \"t=open('/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/eth_audit/paper.txt').read().split('\\n'); print(t[L-1]); print(sum(1 for x in t[:L-1] if '\\f' in x)+1)\"` — note a form feed may sit at the start of a line, so count lines containing '\\f' before line L carefully and state your counting rule.\n3. The two audits: `/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/eth_audit/statement_audit.md` and `proof_audit.md`, plus `closure_modules.json` beside them.\n4. The replay logs: `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/replay/` (README.md, counts.sh, logs/run1, logs/run2, logs/nanoda) and the fetched related-work texts under `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/related/fetched/`, and the Lean companion logs `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/lean/*.log`, `paper3/lean/README.md`. Our own Lean files `/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/PrimitiveMachine.lean` and `Frame.lean` may be read (cat only).\n5. Arithmetic: recompute every number you can with `python3 -I` (rho(n)/n at 49, 50, 100, 1000; the peak 16/e^2 at ln(n+16)=e^4; the return below 1 near ln(n+16)=5503.7; the digit count of e^5504; 2^(rho(n)-n) at 50, 100, 500; the clause-count bound sum_{j<=k} C(2n,j) at n=125,k=3; anything else the paper states as a computed value).\n\nWhat to file, one finding each, with page number (of the PDF), the section, the exact sentence, what you checked, what you found, and a severity (A = a factual disagreement with a source or a wrong line/page number or a wrong number; B = a number or quotation with no stated source or regenerate command; C = a sentence that reads as a debunking or an overclaim beyond what the Lean statement supports; D = out of scope, i.e. any sentence about graphs, pathwidth, treewidth, MOSP, width parameters, crossovers or reductions into width problems — the directory name `SubexpPathwidth` and the manuscript's own quoted corollary objects are allowed, anything else is not; E = the title altered, shortened, re-capitalised or reworded anywhere in the PDF, including running headers and the metadata; F = plain-English stalls: a term used before it is glossed, a sentence a layperson cannot follow, an internal inconsistency between sections (e.g. the same quantity given two values); G = anything else, e.g. a broken cross-reference, a figure whose caption contradicts its axes, a bibliography entry whose details look wrong). Check specifically and report the outcome even when it is \"agrees\": (i) every cited comparator line number (the paper cites many: SAT 13–51, encoding 53–81, Trace 87–90, PrimitiveMachine 92–99, Cfg 103–105, step 107–119, init 121–124, runtimeScale 132–134, runtimeBound 136–139, countWord 147, LocatedCfg..visitedSpace 149–189, the theorem 194–217, sorry 218, and others); (ii) every manuscript quotation's page and line; (iii) the proof's constants (A = 256 + A_t, the witnesses C + 28700, A + 1, S + 5022741, d + 2, e + 2 at Final.lean line 41, cutoff at NativeLargeEntry.lean line 50) at the cited lines; (iv) the replay numbers (3,091 modules, 33 min 6 s, 0 error, 0 sorry, 11 warnings, the axioms line, 95,176 declarations, 110 s, export size 2,355,666,449 bytes / 43,633,742 lines, lean4export v4.34.0, nanoda 0.4.31 commit 8de7e0c4) against the replay logs; (v) the closure numbers (3,091 modules, 550,551 lines, 3,977 family files, 886 outside the closure, 50 Mathlib modules, the keyword counts, 413/2/3 of 418 JSONs, 42 manifest packages, 23 patches) against the audits and the clone where you can recount cheaply (e.g. `find ... -name '*.lean' | wc -l`, `ls lean/ComparatorChallenges/*.json | wc -l`, `grep -L enable_nanoda`, `grep -c '\"enable_nanoda\": false'`); (vi) the related-work quotations against the fetched files; (vii) the Lean companion claims against the two Lean files and the logs; (viii) the measurement section's numbers against `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/tables/practitioner_raw.csv` and `practitioner_meta.json` (those two data files you may read); (ix) whether every number in the text names a section, table, script or log that regenerates it; (x) readability: list every sentence over 45 words and every term used before its gloss, concisely.\n\nAlso check the abstract's word count claim if the paper states one, and that the conclusion's sorting of ledger entries (if it gives counts) is internally consistent.\n\nBe thorough and concrete: a finding without the exact sentence and the exact source line is useless. Do not pad with praise. Write the report to `/tmp/paper3_refuter/REPORT.md` with a one-paragraph summary at the top (counts by severity), then the findings numbered R1, R2, ... grouped by severity A–G, then a short list of what you checked that agreed (so the reader knows the coverage). Return the same report as your final message."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":998,"cache_read_input_tokens":147858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":998,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33d18ed-7e5b-4d5f-8bbe-6467cd7c6364","uuid":"abe016d2-6012-43e9-98f0-280bbc40464b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:51:15.769Z","request_id":"req_011CgjR45hQSKjx2WDZPY4z4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0164ZPMHw4itNiUbhdFh8VX2":{"description":"Refuter pass over paper 3 PDF","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are the refuter for a paper. You read the finished PDF only, check every checkable claim in it against the primary sources listed below, and file every disagreement. You EDIT NOTHING: write no file except your report at `/tmp/paper3_refuter/REPORT.md`. You are deliberately blind to the paper's LaTeX sources, scripts and progress notes: do NOT open anything under `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/*.tex`, `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/scripts/`, `/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/`, or any `reports/*.md` other than the two audits named below. Read the PDF and the primary sources, nothing else.\n\nThe paper: `/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/main.pdf` (62 pages). Start with `mkdir -p /tmp/paper3_refuter && pdftotext -layout /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/main.pdf /tmp/pap