ed statement negates each one. The two sentences the manuscript adds\nat lines 191–194, on unconditional lower bounds for restricted proof systems and on Williams’s\n2016 MA-SETH protocol, are context, not claims about the result.\n\n§1.1.3 (p. 5, lines 213–243). After a list of lower bounds proved from ETH or SETH (lines 213–\n225), the manuscript writes: “Our refutation of ETH and SETH removes one basis for the hard-\nness claims above. Some of the same lower bounds follow from weaker hypotheses that may\n\n                                                 16\n\fstill hold” (lines 226–227). It names the Orthogonal Vectors Conjecture, a hypothesis about\na different problem (lines 229–232), and the hypothesis that unrestricted CNF-SAT admits no\n2(1−δ)n poly(n, m) algorithm, adding: “Theorem 1.1 gives a running-time guarantee for each fixed\nclause width k, while this hypothesis allows the width to grow with n” (lines 235–236). These\nare paper-only remarks in the sense that nothing about any other hypothesis or any reduction is\nin the library; they are also the manuscript’s own statement of what the result does not do, and\nSection 6 rests on them. The one positive transfer, Set Splitting with sets of size at most k by one\nvariable per element and two clauses per set (lines 237–243), is supported in the same sense as\nCorollary 1.3: an encoding on paper into the verified counter, inheriting ρ(n). The caveat at p. 2,\nlines 95–99, that 2o(n) bounds “do not transfer under general polynomial-time reductions,” is not\na claim but a limit the manuscript places on its own result; it is quoted again in Section 6.\n\n3.6     What the library carries beyond the comparator statement\n“Paper-only” is defined against the whole library at commit 4eaee875, not only against the com-\nparator file, so we say what else the library proves about this family. The file SqrtLogSpace/\nFinal.lean (201 lines) states five theorems, each followed by a #print axioms command,\nwhich asks Le