{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZU23fMjapW3t8TnAd1qkJ","type":"tool_result","content":"References\nammkrn. nanoda_lib: an external type checker for Lean 4, written in Rust. https://github.\n  com/ammkrn/nanoda_lib, 2026. Repository README, master branch, commit 8de7e0c4\n  (29 October 2026), version 0.4.31, fetched 5 November 2026.\n\nArmin Biere, Tobias Faller, Katalin Fazekas, Mathias Fleury, Nils Froleyks, and Florian\n  Pollitt. CaDiCaL 2.0. In Computer Aided Verification (CAV 2024), volume 14681 of Lec-\n  ture Notes in Computer Science, pages 133–152. Springer, 2024. doi: 10.1007/978-3-031-\n  65627-9_7. Venue from memory; DOI checked against Crossref on 2026-11-05 (item 10,\n\n\n                                                 51\n\f  paper3/scripts/check_refs.py). The version run is 1.9.5, the one python-sat 1.9.dev15\n  bundles as cadical195.\n\nMarco L. Carmosino, Jiawei Gao, Russell Impagliazzo, Ivan Mihajlin, Ramamohan Paturi, and\n Stefan Schneider. Nondeterministic extensions of the Strong Exponential Time Hypothesis\n and consequences for non-reducibility. In 7th Innovations in Theoretical Computer Science Confer-\n ence (ITCS 2016), pages 261–270, 2016. doi: 10.1145/2840728.2840746. Entry copied from the\n manuscript’s reference list, extract lines 3686–3688; DOI checked against Crossref on 2026-11-05\n (item 10, paper3/scripts/check_refs.py).\n\nSupratik Chakraborty, Kuldeep S. Meel, and Moshe Y. Vardi. A scalable approximate model\n  counter. In Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2013), volume 8124 of\n  Lecture Notes in Computer Science, pages 200–216. Springer, 2013. doi: 10.1007/978-3-642-\n  40627-0_18. Venue from memory; DOI checked against Crossref on 2026-11-05 (item 10,\n  paper3/scripts/check_refs.py). Package pyapproxmc 4.4.0 (Mate Soos), https://\n  github.com/meelgroup/approxmc.\n\nParinya Chalermsook, Marek Cygan, Guy Kortsarz, Bundit Laekhanukit, Pasin Manurangsi,\n  Danup