fs.bib` says all this.\n- **Owner may change**: strike \"Venue from memory\" now that each entry\n  has a checked DOI; or remove the thirteen DOIs if the download rule\n  was meant to exclude registry queries (then 08c's state is restored\n  by `git checkout` of `refs.bib`).\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper3/README.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"## The replay\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"- **The bibliography** (item 10): `python3 paper3/scripts/check_refs.py`\n  (from the repository root; it imports paper 1's checker) fetches the\n  Crossref or DataCite record of every `refs.bib` entry that carries a\n  DOI and compares title, year and first author; `--lookup` also\n  searches Crossref for the entries that have none; `--refresh` ignores\n  the cache `paper3/latex/data/doi_check.json`. The run of record is\n  `paper3/latex/doi_check.log`: 22 entries, 15 with a DOI, 0 disagree\n  (Mertens 2006 accepted as `known`, see the script). Thirteen DOIs were\n  found and added by item 10 (`ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD` 10a); Dinur 2016 is an\n  ECCC report with none; the manuscript, the arXiv record and the four\n  repository READMEs carry none by nature.\n\n## The replay\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\ns=s.replace(\"| `refuter/` | item 10's refuter report |\",\"| `refuter/` | item 10's refuter pass: `README.md` (the blind reading of the whole PDF against the clone, the extract, the audits and the replay logs, every finding with what was done about it) |\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n 'refuter' paper3/README.md","description":"Record entry 10a and the bibliography paragraph in the README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1969,"cache_read_input_tokens":157666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1969,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transfor