pment is MIT-licensed as described in the file LICENSE.\n    23\t\n    24\tNothing below is proved: the file contains definitions only (the canonical encoding of a CNF\n    25\tover `Fin n`, the `PrimitiveMachine` multi-tape model over Mathlib's `Turing.TM0.Stmt` and\n    26\t`Turing.Tape`, its `Trace`, the located configuration that monitors the visited cells, and the\n    27\truntime bound `C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16))`). The namespaces are\n    28\tkept as in the source so that `SubexpCount` reads character for character as the comparator.\n    29\tEverything after this comment block is the copy.\n    30\t-/\n    31\timport Mathlib\n    32\t\n    33\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.BinaryArithmetic\n    34\t\n    35\tdef bitVal (b : Bool) : ℕ := if b then 1 else 0\n=== byte diff of copy (lines 31-221) vs comparator 1-190 + 220\n  191 /tmp/paper3_refuter/cmp_a.txt\n  191 /tmp/paper3_refuter/cmp_b.txt\n  382 total\nIDENTICAL\n=== sorry/axiom in our two files\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean:0\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/PrimitiveMachine.lean:1\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean:13:  never proved and never an axiom**: one fixed primitive multi-tape machine exactly counts the\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean:83:character. Never proved here, never an axiom. -/\n=== toolchain/mathlib of our lib\nleanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2\n1192d6246b","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0164ZPMHw4itNiUbhdFh8VX2","agent_id":"a97cfc7d4ba482ba5","session_id":"e33d18ed-7e5b-4d5f-8bbe-6467cd7c6364","uuid":"318009a1-5d06-4a90-a2a3-13136d1d179d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:57:36.053Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017vjQrA8AFHwijR26eoA6CQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refuter pass over paper 3 PDF"}
