{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtnCWkwnf822GqY7VH8Bm6","type":"tool_result","content":"===== axiom_check.lean\n/-\nAxiom audit for paper 3 (Section 8, \"The statement in our Lean\"): every declaration the\npaper cites from our companion Lean, printed with the axioms it depends on. The two files are\n`lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/PrimitiveMachine.lean` (the verbatim copy of the\ncomparator's machine model, definitions only) and `lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/\nFrame.lean` (the restatement `SubexpCount` and the lemmas about it). The owner's decision of\n2026-11-05 (`paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, S3 resolved) keeps the files where loop0014 wrote them.\n\nExpected: `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` on every line that names a theorem, and\nnothing beyond those three on any line; `sorryAx` on none. The `def`s (`SubexpCount`,\n`ExactCountAndSat`, `IsSubexpExponent`, and the copied `runtimeScale`, `runtimeBound`) are\nprinted to show that they elaborate against the built library; a `def` of a `Prop` is not a\nclaim, and none of them is proved here. Unlike `paper1/axiom_check.lean` there is no control\nline that must show `sorryAx`: the acceptance rule of this paper is that every line is on the\nthree standard axioms, and the committed log is `paper3/lean/axiom_check.log`.\n\n    cd lean && lake env lean ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean > ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.log\n\nNot under `lean/MOSPFormalization/`, so `lake build` does not see it. Nothing of the OpenAI\ncollection is imported: `MOSPFormalization` is our library, and the `OAI.…` names below are\nthe copied definitions inside it.\n-/\nimport MOSPFormalization\n\nopen MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\n\n-- The copied definitions the statement rests on (PrimitiveMachine.lean, the verbatim copy).\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT.count\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.encodeCNF\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.formulaBitLength\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.PrimitiveMachine.step\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.Trace\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.countWord\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.locatedStep\n#print axioms OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.visitedSpace\n\n-- The restatement (Frame.lean): two `Prop`s, never proved, never axioms.\n#print axioms SubexpCount\n#print axioms ExactCountAndSat\n\n-- What is proved about them (Frame.lean).\n#print axioms SubexpCount.anti\n#print axioms ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount\n#print axioms IsSubexpExponent\n#print axioms runtimeBound_eq\n#print axioms tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt\n#print axioms runtimeScale_isLittleO\n#print axioms isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale\n#print axioms LocatedCfg.monitor_config\n#print axioms Trace.config_of_locatedStep\n===== axiom_check.log\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT.count' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.encodeCNF' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.formulaBitLength' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.PrimitiveMachine.step' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.Trace' does not depend on any axioms\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.countWord' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.locatedStep' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.visitedSpace' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.SubexpCount' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.ExactCountAndSat' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.SubexpCount.anti' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.IsSubexpExponent' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.runtimeBound_eq' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.runtimeScale_isLittleO' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.LocatedCfg.monitor_config' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.Trace.config_of_locatedStep' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n===== rediff.log\npaper3/scripts/lean_rediff.py -- 2026-11-05 05:29 UTC\nclone: /home/al/dev/untrusted/openai-math at commit 4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae (expected 4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae)\nsha256 comparator (clone) : 4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685 (expected 4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685)\nsha256 PrimitiveMachine.lean: 23f7926e4644c9640ac815c35152caab9c3ccc64aef6b65266b738e9fffc54c9\nsha256 Frame.lean           : ad24111185ab388675a673b96c930d56adf3f1de15d01184dc01447c35e40fd4\ncomparator file: 220 lines; PrimitiveMachine.lean: 221 lines; Frame.lean: 268 lines\ncheck 1: our copy starts at PrimitiveMachine.lean line 31 (191 lines); expected = clone lines 1-190 + 220 (191 lines)\ncheck 1: byte-identical (diff empty)\ncheck 2: SubexpCount body = Frame.lean lines 85-107 (23 lines); exact_count_and_sat body = clone lines 195-217 (23 lines, `:= by` removed)\ncheck 2: identical after whitespace normalisation (1073 characters)\ncheck 2: identical line by line after stripping indentation (23 lines); the indentation differs by two spaces (a `def` body against a `theorem` type)\ncheck 2: indentation offset (ours minus clone) per line: [-2]\ncheck 3: PrimitiveMachine.lean: 0 `sorry`, 0 `axiom` declaration(s) outside the header comment\ncheck 3: Frame.lean: 0 `sorry`, 0 `axiom` declaration(s) outside the header comment\ncheck 3: the clone's comparator file has `sorry` at line(s) [218]\ncheck 3: the `sorry` line is inside the copied range: False\nALL CHECKS PASSED\n===== README.md\n# The companion Lean of paper 3\n\n*Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.*\n\nPaper 3's Section 8 (\"The statement in our Lean\"). Nothing here is a Lean\nsource file of its own beyond the audit: the companion Lean is two files of\nour library, left where loop0014 wrote them by the owner's decision of\n2026-11-05 (`paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, S3 resolved: \"leave the Lean where it\nis\"; the original brief of item 07, which moved them to\n`lean/MOSPFormalization/ETH/`, is superseded, entry 07a).\n\n## The files\n\n| file | what it is | lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/PrimitiveMachine.lean` | a verbatim copy of lines 1–190 and 220 of `lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` in the OpenAI collection (commit `4eaee875`, SHA-256 `4183b205…`), after a 30-line header (source, commit, hash, Apache 2.0 licence). Definitions only: the formulas and their count, the canonical encoding, the multitape `PrimitiveMachine`, `Trace`, `runtimeScale` (ρ(n) = n (ln ln(n+16))² / √ln(n+16)), `runtimeBound`, `countWord`, the located configuration, `locatedStep`, `visitedSpace`. The theorem and its `sorry` (clone lines 191–219) are not copied. | 221; the copy is lines 31–221 |\n| `lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean` | `SubexpCount (k : ℕ) : Prop` (lines 84–107), the comparator theorem's body character for character; `ExactCountAndSat : Prop := ∀ k, 2 ≤ k → SubexpCount k` (110); the lemmas `SubexpCount.anti` (113), `ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount` (119), `IsSubexpExponent` (125), `runtimeBound_eq` (128), `tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt` (132), `runtimeScale_isLittleO` (144), `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale` (163), `LocatedCfg.monitor_config` (169), `Trace.config_of_locatedStep` (180). Lines 192–268 belong to the other study and are not cited by the paper. | 268 |\n\nBoth files are imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean` (lines 76–77) and\nbuilt by `lake build` in `lean/`; the loop's gate checks after every session\nthat the whole library has no `sorry` and no `axiom` declaration.\n\n## The names the paper cites\n\nAppendix A of the paper (`paper3/latex/secA_appendix_lean.tex`), eight rows:\nthe copied vocabulary (ten `OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.…` names),\n`SubexpCount`, `ExactCountAndSat`, `SubexpCount.anti` with\n`ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount`, `runtimeBound_eq`, `tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt`\nwith `runtimeScale_isLittleO`, `IsSubexpExponent` with\n`isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`, `LocatedCfg.monitor_config` with\n`Trace.config_of_locatedStep`. All under the namespace\n`MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth` except the copy, whose namespaces are the\nsource's.\n\n## The audit\n\n`axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of those 21 declarations, in the pattern\nof `paper1/axiom_check.lean` (without its `sorryAx` control line: this paper's\nacceptance rule is that every line is on the three standard axioms, entry\n07b). Run from `lean/`:\n\n```bash\ncd lean && lake env lean ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean > ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.log\n```\n\n`axiom_check.log` is the committed output (2026-11-05 05:30 UTC, repository\ncommit `95eb564a0`, Lean 4.34.0-rc2 commit `6a10ac8c`, Lake 5.0.0, Mathlib\n`1192d6246b46` from `lean/lake-manifest.json` — our library's toolchain, not\nthe clone's `v4.34.1` / `d13f23b7`): 19 lines on exactly\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; `Computation.Trace` on no axiom\n(an inductive definition); `SqrtLogSpace.countWord` on `[propext, Quot.sound]`;\n`sorryAx` on none.\n\n## The re-diff\n\n`python3 -I paper3/scripts/lean_rediff.py` (from the repository root; `--check`\nverifies without writing) reads the clone with `open()` only and writes\n`rediff.log`:\n\n1. **the copy**: our lines 31–221 against the clone's lines 1–190 followed\n   by 220, byte for byte — identical (191 lines each side, diff empty); the\n   clone's SHA-256 and commit as the header records;\n2. **the statement**: the body of `SubexpCount` (Frame.lean 85–107) against\n   the body of `exact_count_and_sat` (clone 195–217, `:= by` removed) —\n   identical after whitespace normalisation (1,073 characters) and line by\n   line after stripping indentation (23 lines; ours sit two columns further\n   left, a `def` body against a `theorem` type);\n3. **no `sorry`, no `axiom`** in either of our files outside the header\n   comment; the clone's one `sorry` is at line 218, outside the copied range.\n\nExit status is non-zero if any check fails.\n\n## What this does not claim\n\n`SubexpCount k` is a `def` of a `Prop`, never proved here and never an axiom;\nthe copy is definitions only (the proof's 3,091 modules are not copied); no\n`#eval` can evaluate `runtimeScale` (it is `noncomputable`, over real\nlogarithms — every number in the paper's