+2 / e+2, the cutoff, every comparator line number, every manuscript page/line but one, every replay and nanoda number, every related-work quotation, the Lean companion claims, and all of Table 7.1) agree with the sources. Findings: **A: 6** (one false sentence about where \"ETH\" occurs in the Lean, one wrong manuscript page, a line-count artefact of +1 per file, a 41-vs-42 dependency count, two imprecise line citations); **B: 4**; **C: 1**; **D: 0**; **E: 0**; **F: 5**; **G: 5**. No finding touches the paper's stance or its verdict on the proof.\n\nCounting rule used for manuscript pages: `page(L) = 1 + (number of lines before line L that contain a form feed)`; form feeds sit at the start of lines 53, 104, 155, 208, 260, ... (67 in all, 3,815 lines). Under the alternative rule (count form feeds in lines up to and including L) every cited page comes out the same, including the one disagreement below.\n\n---\n\n## A — factual disagreements, wrong line/page numbers, wrong numbers\n\n**R1 (A).** p. 16, §3.5: *\"The hypotheses themselves are not defined in the library (the strings \"ETH\" and \"SETH\" occur in the collection's Lean only in two files of a different family, lean/OAI/Combinatorics/ParityLifts/, which take an ETH-like proposition as a hypothesis and are not among the files the proof depends on, its closure, Section 4).\"* Checked with `grep -rnw ETH` over `lean/**/*.lean`. The string \"ETH\" occurs, besides the two ParityLifts files, in **six files of this family**, all inside comments: `SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean:6` (\"the unchanged ETH square-root-log time scale\"), `SqrtLogSpace/NativeOuterBudgets.lean:147`, `SqrtLogSpace/NativeQueryTimeBounds.lean:49`, `SqrtLogSpace/BooleanDifferences.lean:7` and `:228`, `SqrtLogSpace/NativeHashQueries.lean:377`; and the theorem name `exact_count_eth` (Final.lean:104) contains it in lower case. \"SETH\" indeed occurs nowhere as a word. The substantive point (no hypothesis is defined in the library) stands; the sentence as